<|SECTION:DRAFT REPLY|>
The story's director wrote the following draft reply to the player. The player wants to steer the story without learning what will happen.

```draft
{{ draft }}
```
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
<|SECTION:TASK|>
Rewrite the draft reply for the player. Remove or vaguely paraphrase anything the player has not already witnessed in the scene above:

- Planned or future events, or hints at their nature
- Arc/beat positions, structure, or how much of the story remains
- Hidden roles, motives, secrets or relationships not yet shown in the scene
- Menus of possible outcomes ("I could do X or Y - which do you prefer?") - replace with a vague confirmation that the director will act
- Details of things the director created or changed, beyond what the player themselves asked for
- Hidden state changes or dice results the player has not seen

Keep: acknowledgments, tone, any questions that do not reveal hidden information, and everything the player already knows from the scene. Keep it to one short reply. Preserve the draft's light markdown style.

If the draft reveals nothing, return it unchanged.

Respond with the rewritten reply wrapped in <REDACTED></REDACTED> tags. Respond with nothing else.
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
